WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.240
A fearless future chief, a crazy rooster,
and an egotistical demi-god are just some

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.459
of the cool characters you'll find in Moana.

00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:09.690
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.780
So, what else can you expect from Disney's
latest animated feature?

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.330
Well, when it comes to animation, Moana is
truly beautiful.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:21.019
There's a lush-ness to the islands, and everything
looks suitably inviting, at least when it's

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:25.400
meant to, especially the ocean, which even
takes on its own playful personality throughout

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.400
the film.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.900
And there are also some gorgeous sequences
which have a 2-D animated, handmade, textured

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.230
feel to them, which I really loved.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:38.640
When it comes to the bringing to life the
movie's lead, newcomer Auli'i Cravalho gives

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.190
a fabulously spirited and engaging performance
as the adventurous teen Moana, and, wow, she

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:48.190
can really carry a tune as she more than shows
with her rendition of the soon-to-be-classic,

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.350
How Far I'll Go.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.500
Dwayne Johnson has the bags of personality
and presence needed to pull off the role of

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.350
the super-full-of-himself, shapeshifting demi-god,
Maui.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:00.920
Johnson is wonderfully funny, delivers his
lines with great gusto, and gets one hell

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.150
of a song in the very catchy 'You're Welcome'.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:08.049
And together Cravalho and Johnson make a lovely
on-screen double act, sharing some nice back-and-forth

00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:09.960
as well as a few poignant moments.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.880
As Moana's animal sidekick, Heihei the Rooster,
Alan Tudyk gets some lovely comic scenes,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.229
with a particular emphasis on slapstick.

00:01:17.229 --> 00:01:21.759
And after his roles in the likes of Big Hero
6, Frozen, and Zootopia, he's quickly becoming

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:25.170
Disney's equivalent of Pixar's good-luck-charm,
John Ratzenberger.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.960
And Rachel House is a very welcome presence
as Moana's grandmother, who brings some delightful

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.590
comedy as well as cheeky wisdom to the table.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.299
Jemaine Clement may not get a lot of screen
time as the colossal, blinged-up crab Tamatoa,

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:42.991
but he makes every second count, giving a
truly hilarious, scene-stealing turn that

00:01:42.991 --> 00:01:45.149
just oozes genius comic timing.

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:50.450
Oh, and he gets a brilliant David Bowie-esque
song called 'Shiny', which he completely smashes

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.450
as well!

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:55.350
Actually, on the character front, the only
thing that I was a touch disappointed with

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.009
was that there wasn't more of Moana's pet
pig, Pua, in the film.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:02.999
Story-wise, Moana hits all the beats you'd
expect from this kind of quest-based plot

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:07.420
about a young woman on a mission to save her
people, but keeps things interesting thanks

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:10.459
to its appealing characters and the way it
draws on Polynesian culture.

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:14.870
With veteran Disney directors Ron Clements
and John Musker on board, it's hardly surprising

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:19.250
that Moana takes on elements of some of their
best-known animations, with a good dose of

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.190
The Little Mermaid and a little of Aladdin.

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:25.209
But the directing duo and their screenwriter
Jared Bush, who co-wrote and co-directed the

00:02:25.209 --> 00:02:30.340
amazing Zootopia, also add a inspiration from
elsewhere including Disney's Pinocchio and

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:34.200
even Mad Max: Fury Road
And if you're interested in all of Moana's

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.720
easter eggs and references, I have a video
coming up on that very subject!

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.909
The formula for Moana's story may be tried
and tested, but one of the things that's refreshing

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:46.090
about the movie is the fact that, compared
to many of Disney's princess-based films,

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.239
there's absolutely no love interest here.

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:53.150
So, there's no pining after princes or true
love's kiss for Moana, just lots of adventuring

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.820
on the high seas in an effort to turn around
her people's fortunes before she becomes their

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:58.820
chief.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.939
As far as its music's concerned, Moana is
firing on all cylinders.

00:03:02.939 --> 00:03:06.540
Lin-Manuel Miranda, who created the hit Broadway
musical Hamilton, singer-songwriter Opetaia

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.409
Foa'i, who founded the award-winning group
Te Vaka, and composer Mark Mancina have done

00:03:11.409 --> 00:03:15.360
a cracking job creating a soaring soundtrack
infused with Polynesian spirit.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.920
There are rousing, anthemic tunes, rhythmic
lyrical melodies, jaunty humorous tracks and

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.580
more, and a good many of them are decidedly
ear-wormy.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.849
So, expect to be singing, whistling or humming
these songs long after you've left the movie

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:29.849
theatre!

00:03:29.849 --> 00:03:33.519
In fact, the film's music is so strong that
there's no doubt in my mind that Moana will

00:03:33.519 --> 00:03:38.041
be next on the list of Disney movies adapted
for the stage on Broadway, the West End, and

00:03:38.041 --> 00:03:39.469
all round the world.

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:43.530
In terms of how Moana compares to Disney's
other animations, if your favourites are the

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:48.550
Zootopias and Big Hero 6s of Disney's back
catalogue, then this return to the studio's

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:52.800
more traditional-style of movie may not hit
the heights for you.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.120
But, if you're a fan of films such as Frozen,
then you're very likely to feel right at home

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.120
with this new movie.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:03.379
And, if like me, you like all those films,
then you'll probably find Moana very entertaining

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:04.379
too.

00:04:04.379 --> 00:04:08.659
By the way, if you are a big Disney fan, whatever
you do, make sure you keep your butt in your

00:04:08.659 --> 00:04:12.780
seat right to the very end of the movie's
credits as there is an excellent little scene

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.730
you won't want to miss.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:19.090
And before Moana kicks off, you'll get the
chance to see a new short film called Inner

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:24.380
Workings, which is kind of an Inside Out for
our internal organs instead of our emotions.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:30.100
To sum up: Moana is awash with gorgeous animation,
pitch-perfect voice performances, and a superb

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.850
soundtrack that you're very likely to want
to listen to over and over again.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:37.770
All of this, as well as the film's frequently
funny moments, its refreshingly interesting

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.360
cultural setting, and the big smile it's very
likely to leave on your face make up for the

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.510
fact that on the story side, Moana treads
fairly safe waters.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:48.530
So, I'm giving Moana 4 out of 5 Flicks.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.259
Now, what did you think of Moana?

00:04:50.259 --> 00:04:52.240
And who are your favourite Disney characters?

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.290
Let me know in the comments below!

